  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03SW">Definition <span data-tag="03SW">64.3.10</span>.</a> If $x \in X(k)$ is a rational point and $\bar x : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\bar k) \to X$ the geometric point lying over $x$, we let $\pi _ x : \mathcal{F}_{\bar x} \to \mathcal{F}_{\bar x}$ denote the action by $\text{frob}_ k^{-1}$ and call it the <em>geometric frobenius</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001321473" id="a0001321473-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> </p>
